Below are ten exploratory-to-final BigQuery SQL statements that progressively discover the required fields and finally compute the average score for every board type on 15-Sep-2018 (quick-play completions only).

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at raw rows for 15-Sep-2018.
SELECT * 
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_20180915`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) List all event names that occurred that day.
SELECT DISTINCT event_name
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_20180915`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Show every key that appears inside event_params
--               of quick-play completions (helps locate “board”, “value”, etc.).
SELECT DISTINCT ep.key
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_20180915` AS t,
UNNEST(t.event_params) AS ep
WHERE t.event_name = 'level_complete_quickplay'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Check the different board types recorded.
SELECT DISTINCT ep.value.string_value AS board
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_20180915` AS t,
UNNEST(t.event_params) AS ep
WHERE t.event_name = 'level_complete_quickplay'
  AND ep.key = 'board'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Inspect the score (“value” parameter) captured for completions.
SELECT DISTINCT ep.value.int_value AS score
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_20180915` AS t,
UNNEST(t.event_params) AS ep
WHERE t.event_name = 'level_complete_quickplay'
  AND ep.key = 'value'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Retrieve board/score pairs for a quick manual sanity check.
SELECT
  (SELECT p.value.string_value FROM UNNEST(event_params) AS p WHERE p.key = 'board')  AS board,
  (SELECT p.value.int_value   FROM UNNEST(event_params) AS p WHERE p.key = 'value')  AS score
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_20180915`
WHERE event_name = 'level_complete_quickplay'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Count how many quick-play completions happened per board.
SELECT
  (SELECT p.value.string_value FROM UNNEST(event_params) AS p WHERE p.key = 'board') AS board,
  COUNT(*) AS completions
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_20180915`
WHERE event_name = 'level_complete_quickplay'
GROUP BY board
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Compute the average score each board produced (core logic).
SELECT
  (SELECT p.value.string_value FROM UNNEST(event_params) AS p WHERE p.key = 'board')  AS board,
  AVG( (SELECT p.value.int_value FROM UNNEST(event_params) AS p WHERE p.key = 'value') ) AS avg_score
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_20180915`
WHERE event_name = 'level_complete_quickplay'
GROUP BY board
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Same as #8 but ordered so the “most effective” boards appear first.
SELECT
  board,
  AVG(score) AS avg_score
FROM (
  SELECT
    (SELECT p.value.string_value FROM UNNEST(event_params) AS p WHERE p.key = 'board')  AS board,
    (SELECT p.value.int_value   FROM UNNEST(event_params) AS p WHERE p.key = 'value')  AS score
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_20180915`
  WHERE event_name = 'level_complete_quickplay'
)
GROUP BY board
ORDER BY avg_score DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Final concise answer – average score per board on 15-Sep-2018.
SELECT
  board,
  AVG(score) AS average_score
FROM (
  SELECT
    (SELECT p.value.string_value FROM UNNEST(event_params) AS p WHERE p.key = 'board')  AS board,
    (SELECT p.value.int_value   FROM UNNEST(event_params) AS p WHERE p.key = 'value')  AS score
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_20180915`
  WHERE event_name = 'level_complete_quickplay'
)
GROUP BY board
ORDER BY average_score DESC;
```
